//? Title: Earliest-Deadline-First: Actual Jobs, Preemption and Boundary Deadlines
//? Subtitle: Periodic task timelines, exact utilization and retained backlog in native C++
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given recurring jobs with execution budgets and deadlines, we want one
processor to complete every job on time. A task may be ready while
another is running, so its scheduling priority must account for when
its current job is due. Earliest-deadline-first chooses the nearest
absolute deadline. We inspect an actual preemption, retain the original
three-task hyperperiod, compare EDF and fixed priorities, and check
exact work families. The implementation keeps overdue jobs, checks
horizon-boundary deadlines and tests utilization without a tolerance.
)

\toc

> A newly released job can preempt the running job

Let T7 have period four and cost one, and T99 period ten and cost six.
Both release at zero. T7 runs first, then T99 executes three units.
At time four, the next T7 job is due at eight, earlier than T99's
deadline ten. EDF preempts T99, runs T7 for one unit, then resumes T99.
The ten-unit trace below records the actual selected job ids. Task ids
are labels; input position breaks priority ties.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/edf_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::rt_trace({{7,4,1},{99,10,6}},10);
  std::print("Tiny: {} jobs; busy units {}; idle units {}; preemptions {}; deadline missed {}.\n\n",t.jobs.size(),t.work.busy_ticks,t.work.idle_ticks,t.work.preemptions,t.schedule.deadline_missed);
  std::print("| unit start | selected job | selected task |\n| ---: | :--- | :--- |\n");
  const auto idle=std::numeric_limits<std::size_t>::max();
  for(std::size_t k=0;k<t.tick_jobs.size();++k){const auto id=t.tick_jobs[k];if(id==idle)std::print("| {} | idle | idle |\n",k);else std::print("| {} | {} | T{} |\n",k,id,t.tasks.at(t.jobs.at(id).task_index).id);}
  const auto old=t.tick_jobs.at(3),selected=t.tick_jobs.at(4);const auto& a=t.jobs.at(old);const auto& b=t.jobs.at(selected);
  const auto remaining=[&](std::size_t id){return t.tasks.at(t.jobs.at(id).task_index).wcet-std::count(t.tick_jobs.begin(),t.tick_jobs.begin()+4,id);};
  std::print("\nAt t=4: old job {} has {} units remaining, deadline {}; selected job {} has {} unit remaining, deadline {}.\n",old,remaining(old),a.deadline,selected,remaining(selected),b.deadline);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=5.1;box.height=1.9;box.font_size=23;
  d.node("old",{0,0},std::format("job {}: T{}\nremaining {}\ndeadline {}",old,t.tasks.at(a.task_index).id,remaining(old),a.deadline),box);
  box.fill={187,247,208};d.node("new",{7,0},std::format("job {}: T{}\nremaining {}\ndeadline {}",selected,t.tasks.at(b.task_index).id,remaining(selected),b.deadline),box)
   .node("run",{3.5,-4},std::format("actual unit [4,5)\nrun job {}\nT{}",selected,t.tasks.at(b.task_index).id),box)
   .edge("new","run","earlier deadline").text({3.5,2.3},"At time four, the new job preempts the unfinished job",25).save_svg("build/edf_tiny.svg");
}
```
